// attach to baker girl
Narrator: Clara calls out to a pair who are packing items into crates.
Clara: Hey Keira, Kiara! How are the supply preparations progressing? #portrait:Clara
Keira: Good! At least so far. Supplies have been steadily moving up the mountains, however…
Kiara: We’re a bit worried about the weather.
Kiara: Superstition aside, the rain would make it dangerous to go uphill. But we’ll keep you posted!
Clara: Thanks! #portrait:Clara
Narrator: Keira and Kiara finish nailing a crate closed and walk off, looking like they’re off to do something important.
Noelle: Superstition? #portrait:NoelleSkeptical
Clara: Hm… how much do you know about Noah's tale? #portrait:Clara
Narrator: Clara explains that after Noah's altercation with the Great Disaster, those on Thavmia have been split between damning his actions and regarding it as an unfortunate fall of events.
Clara: I'll spare you from the politics — things have calmed down after five-hundred years, but now that the floods are coming and the weather is strangely bad… #portrait:Clara
Noelle: (People must be wondering if the storms are an answer to Noah's actions.) #portrait:NoelleUm
Noelle: So it doesn't normally storm on Thavmia? #portrait:NoelleUm
Clara: No. The most we'd get is heavy rain over the last centuries. #portrait:Clara
Amelia: …You think he’s krakin’ his knuckles? #portrait:AmeliaHappy
Noelle: (Amelia!) #portrait:NoelleSmallSmile
Narrator: Clara snorts, not seeming to take offense.
Clara: In any case, the weather has been… eventful, but at least no one's gotten hurt. #portrait:Clara
Noelle: (The weather and Noah… this is probably putting the human settlement in an awkward position.) #portrait:NoelleSkeptical
Noelle: (I wonder if any of them are direct descendants from that time?) #portrait:NoelleSkeptical
Clara: Let's head west, towards the farm next! #portrait:Clara
